```spl
| inputlookup authentication.csv
| search logon_type="VPN" username="j.park" source_ip="203.0.113.77"
| eval is_failure=if(result="Failure",1,0), is_success=if(result="Success",1,0)
| stats sum(is_failure) as failures sum(is_success) as successes earliest(timestamp_utc) as first_seen latest(timestamp_utc) as last_seen by username source_ip
| where failures>=10 AND successes>=1
```

Illustrative SPL using an uploaded CSV lookup, not executed in Splunk. For production detections, require time-window ordering (failure burst followed by success), tune thresholds, and validate on actual VPN sourcetype and fields.
